En raison du lieu de publication, cette offre d'emploi est disponible uniquement en anglais.




**Your role, your impact**
 As a Functional Owner \- PPM within the Corporate Oracle ERP/EPM Center of Excellence, you'll play a critical role in supporting the design, delivery, optimization, and continuous improvement of Oracle Fusion Project Portfolio Management (PPM) solutions. You'll work closely with Finance, Project Management, Operations stakeholders, Business Analysts , Functional Owners, Solution Architects, and technical teams to support complex projects, enhancements, and ongoing operations. Your ability to understand and challenge business requirements, design and configure Oracle Fusion PPM solutions, lead functional delivery, execute testing, and provide functional leadership will directly contribute to successful project delivery, operational excellence, solution quality, and the continuous evolution of the Oracle application landscape.








**Your day\-to\-day**
* Lead the end\-to\-end functional delivery of complex Oracle Fusion PPM initiatives;
* Partner with business stakeholders and Business Analysts to gather, analyze, challenge, and refine business requirements;
* Translate business requirements into scalable functional designs, configurations, and solution recommendations;
* Facilitate workshops, requirements discussions, and solution design sessions with stakeholders and project teams;
* Configure, maintain, support, and optimize Oracle Fusion PPM solutions across Project Costing, Project Billing, Project Contracts, Revenue Recognition, Capital and Expense Projects, and Project Financial Management;
* Ensure strong functional integration between Oracle Fusion PPM and related Oracle Financials modules, including General Ledger (GL), Accounts Payable (AP), and Accounts Receivable (AR);
* Review solution options and recommend approaches aligned with business objectives, Oracle best practices, and enterprise standards, while identifying opportunities for process and system improvement;
* Collaborate with Solution Architects and Technical Leads to ensure solution quality, sustainability, maintainability, and alignment with enterprise architecture principles;
* Develop and execute functional testing activities, including CRP, SIT, UAT, regression testing, defect management, and solution validation;
* Support impact assessments, release readiness, deployment planning, and Oracle quarterly update activities;
* Produce and maintain functional documentation, specifications, configuration documentation, and supporting materials;
* Provide knowledge transfer, support user adoption activities, mentor Functional Analysts, and contribute to the continuous improvement of Oracle Fusion PPM capabilities.






**Keys to your success**
* Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Business Administration, Accounting, or a related field, or equivalent professional experience;
* Minimum 6 \- 10 years of experience as a Functional Analyst working with Oracle packaged solutions;
* 4 \- 7 years of hands\-on experience with Oracle Fusion Cloud PPM;
* Experience delivering complex enterprise solutions through projects, enhancements, and operational initiatives, including Oracle Fusion PPM configuration, testing, application support, and continuous improvement activities;
* Strong understanding of Oracle Fusion PPM to Financials integrations, including reconciliation to General Ledger;
* Experience delivering complex enterprise solutions through projects, enhancements, and operational initiatives;
* Experience working with business stakeholders and Business Analysts to define, challenge, and translate business requirements into functional solutions, lead functional workstreams, and participate in CRP, SIT, UAT, regression testing, defect management, and release readiness activities;
* Demonstrated expertise in Project Costing, Project Billing, Project Contracts, Project Financial Management, Revenue Recognition, and Capital and Expense Projects;
* Experience documenting functional requirements, specifications, solution designs, configuration approaches, supporting documentation, and mentoring analysts and junior team members;
* Strong analytical, facilitation, problem\-solving, communication, stakeholder management, collaboration, and organizational skills, with the ability to balance strategic thinking and hands\-on functional execution while managing competing priorities.


**Extra edge**
* Oracle Fusion PPM certification;
* Experience serving as a Functional Owner, Domain Lead, or Solution Lead, and providing functional governance, design oversight, and functional sign\-off for major Oracle initiatives;
* Experience working within an internal Oracle Center of Excellence (CoE) operating model, supporting Oracle quarterly updates, release planning, release governance, CRP1, CRP2, SIT, and UAT activities, as well as internal and external audit initiatives related to Oracle PPM and project accounting;
* Experience with OTBI, BI Publisher, Power BI, or Power Query;
* Knowledge of Oracle Financials Cloud and Oracle Enterprise Performance Management (EPM), and understanding of integrations, data conversions, reconciliation processes, data quality practices, project accounting controls, compliance, audit requirements, and advanced Microsoft Excel capabilities.


**Language Skills**
* English: Proficient






**Our mission, your future**
 As a global network of trusted advisors, we create cutting\-edge technological solutions to overcome today’s challenges and anticipate tomorrow’s needs. It all starts with the collaboration of a diverse team of passionate innovators, each driven to make a difference. Together, we challenge the status quo and push each other to new heights.




 Ready to leave your mark on engaging mandates and shape the future through digital transformation and strategic consulting? Take your ambitions to the next level and discover your next exciting challenge with us!








**Our offer**
* Global collaboration: Partner directly with our North American teams on projects for clients in high\-impact industries, gaining the kind of cross\-border exposure that sharpens your expertise and expands your horizons.
* Continuous growth and learning: Unlimited access to online learning, plus certification paths, including through our Microsoft, Oracle, and Salesforce partnerships, so your expertise keeps pace with the technology you work on.
* Flexible work options: Work arrangements that support your rhythm and your reality.
* Support for your well\-being: Comprehensive insurance plan to support you and your family, with premiums fully paid by us.


**Our commitments**
* Our authenticity is our strength: The diversity of our backgrounds, experiences, thoughts and insights is our competitive advantage. We foster a collaborative environment where we embrace our authenticity and leverage our unique perspectives to collectively build the future we all envision.
* An inclusive path to success: Fostering an environment where you can thrive starts with ensuring an accessible recruitment process. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to contact us. For more information, please visit our accessibility page: https://www.alithya.com/en/accessibility .

**Job Description**
 Vice President




 Hyderabad




**About Citco**
 Citco is a global leader in fund services, corporate governance and related asset services with staff across 80 offices worldwide. With more than $1 trillion in assets under administration, we deliver end\-to\-end solutions and exceptional service to meet our clients’ needs.




 For more information about Citco, please visit www.citco.com




**About The Team \& Business Line**
 Fund Administration is Citco’s core business, and our alternative asset and accounting service is one of the industry’s most respected. Our continuous investment in learning and technology solutions means our people are equipped to deliver a seamless client experience.




 As a core member of our Private Equity team, you will be working with some of the industry’s most accomplished professionals to deliver award\-winning services for complex fund structures that our clients can depend upon.




**Your Role**
* Responsible for maintaining books and records and calculation of fund Net Asset Values;
* Coordinating and reviewing financial statements and associated reports, including performance metrics for monthly/quarterly reporting;
* Coordinate and review calculations of carried interest/performance/incentive fees;
* Coordinate and review calculations and investor allocations for capital calls, distributions and equalisations;
* Coordinate and review partner capital account statements;
* Coordinate processing of payments and other transactions;
* Supervise junior staff, reviewing and signing off on work performed;
* Acting as a primary day\-to\-day contact with clients and other fund participants;
* Work closely with the Investor Relations team to respond to investor queries and to disseminate capital activity and other investor notices;
* Maintaining relationships with investors, investment advisors/managers, banks and auditors and other fund participants;
* Assisting auditors and other fund participants and advisers;
* Participating in presentations to existing and prospective clients;
* Monitor compliance of various agreements with clients, including the Service Level Agreement;
* Participating in projects that may be defined from time to time in connection with the continuing expansion and evolution of the business;
* Any other functions required as part of the business of the Company, and reporting to the Senior Vice President.


**About You**
* Minimum of 10 experience in accounting for the financial services sector, particularly Private Equity, Asset Management or Fund Administration.
* Experienced in reviewing and preparing general ledger and financial statements.
* Established knowledge relation to consolidations under IFRS.
* Excellent communication skills and proficiency in English (both verbal and written).
* Motivated, bright and diligent individual who is driven to meet deadlines.
* A team player who is able to manage individual responsibilities.
* Sound judgment, problem solving and analytical skills.
* Proficient with Microsoft Applications (Excel, Word, PowerPoint etc.).
* User experience with enterprise accounting system(s).


**Our Benefits**
 Your wellbeing is of paramount importance to us, and central to our success. We provide a range of benefits, training and education support, and flexible working arrangements to help you achieve success in your career while balancing personal needs. Ask us about specific benefits in your location.




 We embrace diversity, prioritizing the hiring of people from diverse backgrounds. Our inclusive culture is a source of pride and strength, fostering innovation and mutual respect.




 Citco welcomes and encourages applications from people with disabilities. Accommodations are available upon request for candidates taking part in all aspects of the selection.
